From a46a7d048ad8ff7003fa5a866dac1718fe8b5332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenThesis <openthesis@openthesis.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] sentry/platform: add perf_event instruction counter for
 virtual clock advancement

Count retired instructions per task using perf_event_open with
PERF_COUNT_HW_INSTRUCTIONS. The instruction count feeds into the
virtual clock (patch 1) to advance time proportionally, giving
sub-syscall time resolution while remaining fully reproducible
(instruction counts are deterministic when scheduling is deterministic).

On platforms where hardware performance counters are unavailable
(e.g., nested VMs, some cloud instances), the counter gracefully
degrades to a no-op and the virtual clock relies solely on scheduling
quanta for time advancement.

Requirements:
  - Linux x86_64 with perf_event support
  - perf_event_paranoid <= 1 (or CAP_PERFMON)
  - Not available inside nested VMs without PMU passthrough

Integration notes:
  - pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go: after a task's scheduling
    slice completes, read the instruction counter and call
    VirtualClock.AdvanceInstructions(delta).
  - pkg/sentry/platform/kvm/machine.go: create an InstructionCounter
    for each vCPU thread.
  - pkg/sentry/platform/ptrace/ptrace.go: create an InstructionCounter
    for each traced thread.
